 "music": "bed",
 "title": "Why is Redis so fast",
 "sources": [
  "Redis docs, 'Diagnosing latency issues' (https://redis.io/docs/latest/operate/oss_and_stack/management/optimization/latency/, fetched 2026-11-24): 'Redis uses a mostly single threaded design... a single process serves all the client requests, using a technique called multiplexing'; requests are served sequentially; 'designed to not block on system calls, such as reading data from or writing data to a socket'; GET, SET, LPUSH 'are executed in constant (and very small) time'; 'when a request is slow to serve all the other clients will wait'; KEYS 'should only be used for debugging purposes'; SCAN iterates the key space incrementally.",
  "Redis FAQ (https://redis.io/docs/latest/develop/get-started/faq/, fetched 2026-11-24): 'data served from memory, disk used for storage'; Redis is 'usually either memory or network bound'.",
  "Illustration only: the queue squares and client nodes are drawings, not measurements."
 ],
 "lines": [
  {
   "text": "Redis serves every request on a single thread. So, is it slow or fast? Guess now.",
   "caps": "ONE *THREAD | SLOW OR *FAST? | *GUESS NOW"
  },
  {
   "text": "It's fast. All the data lives in memory, so reads never wait on a disk.",
   "caps": "IT'S *FAST | DATA IN *MEMORY | NO *DISK WAIT"
  },
  {
   "text": "One thread means requests run one by one, so they never collide.",
   "caps": "*ONE BY ONE | NEVER *COLLIDE"
  },
  {
   "text": "And it never blocks on the network. Multiplexing lets one thread watch many connections.",
   "caps": "NEVER *BLOCKS | *MULTIPLEXING | MANY *CONNECTIONS"
  },
  {
   "text": "Commands like GET and SET take tiny, constant time, so the queue keeps moving.",
   "caps": "*GET AND SET | *CONSTANT TIME | QUEUE *MOVES"
  },
  {
   "text": "But here's the catch: one slow command makes every other client wait.",
   "caps": "THE *CATCH | ONE *SLOW COMMAND | EVERYONE *WAITS"
  },
  {
   "text": "Like KEYS on a big database. Use SCAN instead, which walks the keys in small steps.",
   "caps": "LIKE *KEYS | USE *SCAN | *SMALL STEPS"
  },
  {
   "text": "So Redis is fast because every request is tiny. Did you guess right?",
   "caps": "EVERY REQUEST *TINY | DID YOU GUESS *RIGHT?"
  }
 ],
